Random decimal number
import numpy as np

print(np.random.random())
Possible output:
0.6472
Run again:
0.2351
It produces values between:
0 and 1
________________________________________
Generate Multiple Random Decimal Numbers
print(np.random.random(5))
Possible output:
[0.12 0.76 0.34 0.91 0.45]
________________________________________
Random Integers
Syntax:
np.random.randint(start, stop)
Example:
print(np.random.randint(1, 10))
Possible output:
7
Important:
Start included
Stop excluded
Therefore:
np.random.randint(1, 10)
can generate:
1 to 9
